Xiaomi/QTI compatibility (ST21NFC_XIAOMI_COMPAT, set in Kbuild; code in
st21nfc_xiaomi.[ch] and "XIAOMI-COMPAT" blocks in st21nfc.c):
  Donor: Xiaomi vendor tree, QTI vendor/st/opensource/driver (ST 2.2.0.19 + QTI)
    https://github.com/sm6225-dev/kernel_xiaomi_sm6225-modules
    branch 16, path st/opensource/driver, subtree commit
    8f94cf63561d42a5a9a0fcebc63128cfcede2943 ("Add 'st/opensource/driver/' from
    commit 'aaebe1dea410a80d187cbf57c9f433d07784ff9f'"), nfc/st21nfc.c blob 7cd9c29a
  Licence: GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE.txt in the donor; QTI copyright
    "Copyright (c) 2022-2023 Qualcomm Innovation Center, Inc.")
  Taken (behaviour active in the stock amethyst stm_nfc_i2c.ko): clkreq GPIO
    made MPM wake-capable via msm_gpio_mpm_wake_set(); clk_get("nfc_ref_clk")
    voting and ST21NFC_CLK_DISABLE_UNPREPARE removed; secure_zone state with
    reset-line gating (always non-secure); probe log lines.
  Not taken: NFC_SECURE_PERIPHERAL_ENABLED (smcinvoke/QTEE secure-zone query
    and NFC_SECURE_ZONE handling), CONFIG_NFC_BOB1 (nvmem) and ST21NFC_ON_OFF;
    none of them is present in the stock binary.
  Cross-reference for the secure-zone code: https://github.com/xiaomi-8550-kernel/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8550-modules
    branch uvite, st/opensource/driver (2.2.0.15, smcinvoke unconditional).
